# Phaser Object Pooling Implementation

## Context
- When creating/destroying many game objects frequently (projectiles, particles, enemies)
- When performance issues occur due to frequent object instantiation and garbage collection
- When implementing systems that need to efficiently recycle game objects
- When creating shooting mechanics, particle effects, or enemy spawning systems

## Requirements
- Use Phaser's built-in Group system for object pooling
- Implement proper object activation and reset functionality
- Minimize object creation during gameplay
- Return objects to the pool rather than destroying them
- Pre-allocate pools during scene initialization or loading
- Implement proper cleanup for pools when scenes shut down

