This implementation creates serious performance issues by constantly creating and destroying objects. Each bullet, enemy, and explosion creates new GameObjects and physics bodies, causing frequent garbage collection. The lack of proper object pooling leads to memory fragmentation and can cause frame rate drops, especially on mobile devices.
