## Phaser-Specific Object Pooling Techniques

### 1. Using Phaser's Group System

Phaser's Group is specifically designed for object pooling:

```typescript
// Create an optimized object pool
const bulletPool = scene.add.group({
  // What type of object to create
  classType: Phaser.GameObjects.Sprite,
  
  // How many objects to pre-create
  maxSize: 30,
  
  // Whether inactive objects should be removed from the display list
  runChildUpdate: false,
  
  // Create callback runs when new objects are created
  createCallback: (obj) => {
    // Setup physics
    scene.physics.world.enable(obj);
    
    // Configure physics properties
    obj.body.setSize(obj.width * 0.5, obj.height * 0.5);
  }
});

// Pre-populate the pool (created objects start inactive)
bulletPool.createMultiple({
  key: 'bullet',
  frame: 0,
  active: false,
  visible: false,
  quantity: 20
});

// Get an object from the pool
const bullet = bulletPool.getFirstDead(true, x, y);

// Return to pool
bullet.setActive(false);
bullet.setVisible(false);
```

