### 3. Using GameObjectFactory for Custom Pooling

```typescript
// Define a factory for creating objects
scene.make.gameObject.add({
  name: 'enemy',
  factory: (config) => {
    return new Enemy(scene, config.x, config.y);
  }
});

// Use factory with pooling
const enemy = enemyGroup.get(100, 200, 'enemy');
```

### 4. Particle System Management

Phaser's particle system already uses pooling internally:

```typescript
// Create a reusable particle manager
const particles = scene.add.particles('particle');

// Create multiple emitters that share the particle pool
const emitter1 = particles.createEmitter({
  // Emitter config
});

const emitter2 = particles.createEmitter({
  // Second emitter config
});

// Manually release particles when needed
emitter1.explode(10, x, y);

// Stop emitting but keep manager alive
emitter1.stop();

// Completely stop and destroy particles
particles.destroy();
```

### 5. Using Arcade Physics Bodies Pooling

For physics-heavy games, body recycling is crucial:

```typescript
// Enable pooling of physics bodies in the scene
scene.physics.world.enableBodySleeping = true;
scene.physics.world.recycleableBodies = true;

// When removing objects
physics.disableBody(sprite.body, true); // Put body back in pool

// When reactivating
physics.enableBody(sprite, 0, 0, true, true);
```

### 6. Custom Group Extensions

Extend Group for specialized pooling behavior:

```typescript
class BulletPool extends Phaser.GameObjects.Group {
  constructor(scene) {
    super(scene, {
      classType: Bullet,
      maxSize: 30
    });
    
    // Custom pool methods
    this.initialize();
  }
  
  initialize() {
    // Pre-populate
    this.createMultiple({
      key: 'bullet',
      active: false,
      visible: false,
      quantity: 30
    });
  }
  
  fireBullet(x, y, vx, vy) {
    const bullet = this.getFirstDead(true, x, y);
    if (bullet) {
      bullet.fire(vx, vy);
      return bullet;
    }
    return null;
  }
}
```

